It's not the same experience.  It's many similar experiences.
The more specific you get with a description, the fewer (in some sense)
experiences match the description.  If there was an exact center of perfect
happiness and you could describe it in infinite detail, maybe there'd only
be one of it.  But if you have a pretty good description, then lots of
experiences would fit the bill, and if you say "at least 50% happy,"
then whole loads of 'em, and "as probably happy as you can get" would
seem a sensible goal if only probability made sense.

 --Steve

